# NOTION MEMORY BANK - PAGE LOCATIONS

**CRITICAL:** This project uses **Notion** as the Memory Bank backend. All read/write operations MUST use Notion MCP tools (`notion-fetch`, `notion-update-page`, `notion-create-pages`), NOT local file operations.

**Language:** All content written to Notion (page body, properties, subtasks, etc.) MUST be in **English**. Chat responses to the user may use the user's language.

## Identifier Convention

- **Projects**: `projectId` in config matches the **Project ID** property in the **Projects** database (numeric value). In JSON you may use a **number** (`123`) or **string** (`"123"`) — both are valid.
- **Tasks**: `taskId` matches **Task ID** (same rule: JSON number or string).

Example: `projectId` `123` or `"123"` → resolve via **Project ID**; `taskId` `588` or `"588"` → resolve via **Task ID**.

**MCP / search:** When passing `projectId` or `taskId` to `notion-search` `query` (or comparing to Notion properties), coerce if needed (e.g. `String(projectId)`) so the value matches Notion’s stored form.

**Task ID in MCP:** **Task ID** may be `auto_increment_id` in Notion; `notion-fetch` can still return it as a **string** in JSON (e.g. `"1430"`). Compare using normalized string or number.

**Issue ID / Issue URL (Tasks):** In the canonical Memory Bank **Tasks** data source, **Issue ID** is typically type **text**. The cell often holds a markdown link `[KEY](https://...)` so **config `issueUrl` is usually parsed from `Issue ID`**, not from a second Notion column. If your workspace adds a separate URL property, see `Core/notion-verification.mdc` step 6.

## Configuration

Read `.cursor/notion-memory-bank.json`:

**Config write format (MUST):** When writing `.cursor/notion-memory-bank.json`, use formatted JSON: 2-space indentation, one key per line. Parse existing content, merge changes, then serialize with `JSON.stringify(obj, null, 2)` – never minified single-line JSON.

**Recommended key order** (see `.cursor/notion-memory-bank.json.example`): **`taskId`**, **`taskName`**, **`taskPageUrl`**, **`issueId`**, **`issueUrl`**; Task subpages **`creativePageUrl`**, **`reflectionPageUrl`**, **`archivePageUrl`**; **`projectId`**, **`projectName`**, **`projectPageUrl`**; Project subpages **`activeContextPageUrl`** through **`styleGuidePageUrl`**; last **`projectsDataSourceUrl` / `tasksDataSourceUrl`** (`collection://` for MCP).

**Migration:** Older configs may still use `activeContextPageId`, `progressPageId`, etc. — migrate those keys to **`activeContextPageUrl`**, **`progressPageUrl`**, … If the old value was a bare Notion page identifier, **`notion-fetch`** it once and store only the canonical **`https://`…** **`url`** in the **`*PageUrl`** field. Missing keys are treated as null. Subpages are created on first use when notion-verification runs (e.g. `/van`). `projectName`, `taskName`, `issueId`, `issueUrl`, `projectPageUrl`, and `taskPageUrl` are populated when notion-verification fetches Project and Task pages. Legacy configs may still contain **`projectsDatabasePageUrl`** / **`tasksDatabasePageUrl`**; they are **not** in the example schema—omit them from new writes and remove them when normalizing config to match **`.cursor/notion-memory-bank.json.example`**.

**`*PageUrl` / `projectPageUrl` / `taskPageUrl` (human-edited JSON):** Store **only** full **`https://`…** Notion page URLs (browser address bar or MCP **`url`** on `notion-fetch`). Do **not** put bare Notion page identifiers in these keys—agents upgrade any legacy bare value to **`https://`…** on the next verification pass.

| Key | Required | Description |
|-----|----------|-------------|
| projectId | Yes | Numeric key: JSON **number** or **string** (e.g. `123` or `"123"`) — must match **Project ID** on the Project row |
| projectName | No | Page title of Project (populated when notion-verification fetches Project) |
| projectPageUrl | No | **`https://`…** Notion URL for the resolved Project page; synced on Project fetch (handy in the JSON file: Ctrl/Cmd+click opens Notion) |
| taskId | No* | Numeric key: JSON **number** or **string** (e.g. `588` or `"588"`) — must match **Task ID** on the Task row; null → `/van [description]` creates one |
| taskName | No | Page title of Task (populated when notion-verification fetches Task) |
| taskPageUrl | No | **`https://`…** Notion URL for the resolved Task page; synced on Task fetch (same editor link behavior) |
| issueId | No | External tracker key from Task's **Issue ID** text (plain key, or link **label** when value is `[KEY](url)`); synced on Task fetch |
| issueUrl | No | Browse URL: parsed from markdown in **Issue ID**, or from optional separate **Issue URL** if the schema has it; synced on Task fetch |
| activeContextPageUrl | No | activeContext subpage: canonical **`https://`…** Notion page URL; if null, create under Project |
| progressPageUrl | No | progress subpage: **`https://`…** URL; if null, create under Project |
| productContextPageUrl | No | productContext subpage: **`https://`…** URL; if null, create under Project (Level 4) |
| systemPatternsPageUrl | No | systemPatterns subpage: **`https://`…** URL; if null, create under Project (Level 4) |
| techContextPageUrl | No | techContext subpage: **`https://`…** URL; if null, create under Project (Level 4) |
| styleGuidePageUrl | No | style-guide subpage: **`https://`…** URL; if null, create under Project (creative UI/UX) |
| creativePageUrl | No | Creative subpage: **`https://`…** URL; if null, create under Task |
| reflectionPageUrl | No | Reflection subpage: **`https://`…** URL; if null, create under Task |
| archivePageUrl | No | Optional archive subpage: **`https://`…** URL; clear when **`taskId`** changes — see **`/van`** Step 2 and **`/change-task`** Step 3 |
| projectsDataSourceUrl | Yes | Projects data source (`collection://...` from `notion-fetch` of the Projects **database**). **MCP** scoped tools need this string—not a browser URL alone. If invalid, recover per `Core/notion-memory-bank-ops.mdc` (**Recover invalid or missing data source URLs**) |
| tasksDataSourceUrl | Yes | Tasks data source (`collection://...` from `notion-fetch` of the Tasks **database**). Same as **projectsDataSourceUrl** |

## Subpage Naming Convention

- **Project subpages** (activeContext, progress, productContext, systemPatterns, techContext, style-guide): Include `projectId` in title. Format: `Active Context <projectId>`, `Progress <projectId>`, etc. (e.g. `Active Context 37` whether `projectId` is `37` or `"37"`). Analogous to Task subpages including taskId. Enables stale detection when page is not under the expected Project.
- **Task subpages** (creative, reflection, archive): Include `taskId` in title. Format: `Creative <taskId>`, `Reflection <taskId>`, `Archive <taskId>` (e.g. `Creative 1391`). Enables stale detection when page is not under the expected Task.

## Subpage body (do not echo page title)

Notion already shows the page **title** at the top. **Do not** put a level-1 heading (`# ...`) in the **body** that duplicates that title—it is redundant.

- **Primary scope:** Project subpages (**activeContext**, **progress**, **productContext**, **systemPatterns**, **techContext**, **style-guide**). **Task** subpages (**Creative**, **Reflection**, **Archive**): same rule—do not open the body with `#` whose text equals the page title; use `##` for the first section unless a command’s workflow explicitly requires a different structure that does not duplicate the title.
- **activeContext / progress** (e.g. `/van`, `/archive`): Start the written body with `##` sections (e.g. `## Current focus (YYYY-MM-DD)`), not `# Active Context <projectId>` or `# Progress <projectId>`.
- **Cleanup**: If `notion-fetch` shows the body opening with `#` whose text matches `properties.title` (same wording, ignoring trivial whitespace), remove that heading (and one following blank line if present) via `notion-update-page` with `command: "update_content"`, preserving the rest.

## Resolving pages (Project, Task, and `*PageUrl`)

**Canonical procedure:** Resolve Project and Task rows using **`Core/notion-verification.mdc` step 4** and (for **Task**) **`Core/notion-task-id-resolution.mdc`**. This section summarizes; it must **not** contradict those rules.

1. **Project:** **`notion-verification.mdc` step 4** — **URL** (**`projectPageUrl`**) **> title** (**`projectName`**); **duplicate project titles** → **`projectId`** / **Project ID** tiebreaker. Then `notion-fetch` with the page URL.
2. **Task:** **`Core/notion-task-id-resolution.mdc`** — **URL** (**`taskPageUrl`**) **> title** (**`taskName`**, project-scoped search + **candidate** fetches). **`taskId`** disambiguates **duplicate titles** and stays in config for Memory Bank invariants; **`/van`** and **`/change-task`** share the same rules. Do **not** use `notion-search` with **`data_source_url`** = `tasksDataSourceUrl` and **`query`** = numeric **`taskId`** as the **sole** resolver. **Note:** If your Tasks database still uses a property named **ID** (not **Task ID**), the MCP key may be `userDefined:ID` — confirm on a `notion-fetch` of a Task row; values are numeric like **Project ID**.
3. **Subpages**: Use the corresponding **`*PageUrl`** **`https://`…** value from config if set; otherwise create under Project or Task with `notion-create-pages`.
4. **`notion-create-pages` parent:** Notion’s create API uses **`parent: { page_id: "…" }`**. Derive that value **only in-session**: `notion-fetch` the parent’s **`https://`…** URL (**`projectPageUrl` / `taskPageUrl`** or resolution result), read the returned **`id`**, pass it as **`page_id`**, and **do not** write that raw value into **`*PageUrl`** / **`projectPageUrl`** / **`taskPageUrl`**—after creating a child, `notion-fetch` the new page and persist its **`https://`…** **`url`** in config.
5. **`notion-fetch` / `notion-update-page` targets:** Use the **`https://`…** string from **`*PageUrl`** (or from resolution) first. If **`notion-update-page`** rejects the URL form, `notion-fetch` that URL, use the returned **`id` only for that tool call**, then **`notion-fetch`** again if you need the canonical **`https://`…** to write back to JSON.

**Resolution failure:** If no row matches after **Project** and **Task** **URL** > **title** resolution (and duplicate-title tiebreaks) in **`notion-verification.mdc`** / **`notion-task-id-resolution.mdc`**, report verification incomplete. Do **not** pick an unrelated row to “force” a match. **Task:** see **`notion-task-id-resolution.mdc`**; **Project:** step 4 **incomplete** ask for **`projectPageUrl`** / **`projectName`** / pasted **URL**.

**Bad data source URLs:** If `projectsDataSourceUrl` / `tasksDataSourceUrl` fail, run recovery in `Core/notion-memory-bank-ops.mdc` before relying on scoped search. See `Core/notion-verification.mdc` step 2.

## Mapping: Notion pages and file-based Memory Bank paths

**Terminology:** **File-based Memory Bank** means the Markdown-at-repo layout: files under `memory-bank/` plus `tasks.md` at the repo root (no Notion backend for those roles). **This repository** uses Notion as the primary surface; the **File-based path** column names the same *role* on disk when using a file-based Memory Bank.

**Primary surface:** the **Notion** page or body in the first column—resolve via config keys and MCP. **This repository** does not use local `memory-bank/*.md` for those roles.

| Notion page / body | File-based path (same role) | Config Key |
|--------------------|---------------------------------------------|------------|
| Current **Task** page body | tasks.md | taskId (number or string, e.g. `588`) |
| **Project** page body | projectbrief.md | projectId (number or string, e.g. `123`) |
| **Active Context** subpage under Project | activeContext.md | activeContextPageUrl |
| **Progress** subpage under Project | progress.md | progressPageUrl |
| **Product Context** subpage under Project | productContext.md | productContextPageUrl |
| **System Patterns** subpage under Project | systemPatterns.md | systemPatternsPageUrl |
| **Tech Context** subpage under Project | techContext.md | techContextPageUrl |
| **Style guide** subpage under Project | style-guide.md | styleGuidePageUrl |
| **Creative** subpage under Task | creative/creative-[name].md | creativePageUrl |
| **Reflection** subpage under Task | reflection/reflection-[id].md | reflectionPageUrl |
| **Archive** subpage under Task (or linked child) | archive/archive-[id].md | optional `archivePageUrl` if used; otherwise resolve via Task child titled `Archive <taskId>` or Task body `<page>` links |

## Active Context: Notion policy and multi-task

The **Active Context** Project subpage (`Active Context <projectId>`, config **`activeContextPageUrl`**) holds **current phase and working focus** per in-flight task—not a substitute for the **Task page body**, the **Progress** subpage, or Task **Creative / Reflection / Archive** subpages. **Several parallel tasks** may appear on this one page; config **`taskId`** still picks the **primary** task for `/van` and task-scoped tools.

### Role and content

- **Purpose:** **Phase and working focus**—what stream of work is active and the immediate direction (e.g. planning vs implementation vs reflection handoff)—**not** an implementation log, checklist, or milestone journal.
- **Where detail lives:** **Task page body** (plan, checklists, status), **Progress** (milestones, observations, build log), **Creative / Reflection / Archive** (design, retro, completion record). **Do not** copy long plan text, file lists, test output, or milestone tables into Active Context; use **short** bullets and optional `<mention-page url="[URL]">[Title]</mention-page>` when a pointer helps.
- **Per-task body:** Under each task heading, keep **only** what fits “current focus”: phase label, next step, blockers, optional task link—typically a **small** number of bullets.

### When to write Active Context (commands)

- **`/van`** and **`notion-verification.mdc` step 6** (after Task resolve): set or refresh **`## Task <taskId> — <taskName>`** for the **resolved primary** task—**focus / phase**, same merge rules as below.
- **`/change-task`:** **add or update only** the **new** primary task’s **`## Task …`** block; **preserve** all other **`## Task …`** sections. **Never** clear the page or `replace_content` the full body for a switch.
- **`/plan`:** update **only** that task’s **`## Task …`** block when loaded level workflow rules require refreshing **planning focus** for the primary task. Otherwise **read** Active Context for context; **do not** duplicate the plan from the Task page here.
- **`/reflect`:** when loaded reflection rules require Memory Bank integration (e.g. Level 4), **optionally** reconcile **only** the primary task’s block with **brief** lines (status, action items, next step)—**do not** paste the Reflection subpage body.
- **`/build`**, **`/creative`:** **do not** use Active Context as the default log; write implementation and design detail to **Task page**, **Progress**, and **Creative**. Touch Active Context only if the **user** asks for a focus change or a loaded rule explicitly requires a **short** focus update for the primary task’s block.
- **`/archive`:** **MANDATORY:** **remove** the archived task’s **`## Task <taskId> — …`** section (from that heading through the line before the next peer `##`) so completed work does not stay in the in-flight list. **Do not** delete other tasks’ sections. Optional: one line under **`## Recently completed`** with `<mention-page>` to **`Archive <taskId>`**.

### Multi-task invariant and merge-safe pattern

- The **Active Context** page (`Active Context <projectId>`) may list **more than one** parallel in-flight task. Config **`taskId`** is the **primary** Task for `/van`, task logs, and single-task resolution; **other** streams exist **only** as extra **`## Task …`** sections—no extra config keys.

**English in Notion; one `##` section per task:**

- `## Task <taskId> — <taskName>` (example: `## Task 588 — Add OAuth callbacks`)
- Under it: **short** bullets (focus / phase, blockers, next step). `<mention-page url="[URL]">[Title]</mention-page>` where helpful.
- **`/van` Step 6:** After `notion-fetch` of Active Context, **add or update only** the section for the resolved **`taskId`** / **`taskName`**. **Preserve** every other **`## Task …`** section. Prefer **`update_content`** with targeted `old_str` / `new_str` (or scoped `replace_content_range`)—**do not** `replace_content` the entire page when multiple task sections exist.
- **Legacy bodies** with only `## Current focus (YYYY-MM-DD)` and no **`## Task …`:** **append** `## Task <taskId> — <taskName>` with the current focus; **do not** clear unrelated legacy sections in the same edit.
- **`notion-verification.mdc` step 6:** Reconcile **only** the resolved **`taskId`** block—do not retitle or re-scope the whole page around one task.

Optional: **`Progress <projectId>`** may mirror a project-wide `## In progress` list (task links and one line each). Same merge discipline—update lines for the relevant task without replacing unrelated entries when possible.

## Page Links in Content

- **Cross-references** (References, progress, activeContext): use `<mention-page url="[URL]">[Title]</mention-page>`
- **Preserving child pages** (replace_content_range): use `<page url="...">` to keep child structure. Do NOT use `<page>` for cross-references – that can move pages.
- **Reflection/Archive under Task:** Use ONLY `<page url="...">`. Do NOT combine with `<mention-page>` – that creates redundant display.

## MCP Tool Usage

- **Read**: Resolve identifier → `notion-fetch` with the **`https://`…** **`*PageUrl`** (or the resolved Project/Task URL from step 4).
- **Update content**: `notion-update-page` with `command: "replace_content"` or `replace_content_range` or `insert_content_after`, targeting the same page as **`notion-fetch`** (see **Resolving pages** item 5 if the URL form is rejected).
- **Create page**: `notion-create-pages` with `parent: { page_id: "<from notion-fetch of parent https URL>" }` and `properties: { title: "..." }`, `content: "..."` (see **Resolving pages** item 4—never persist this **`page_id`** into **`*PageUrl`**; store the child’s **`https://`…** after fetch).
- **MUST output in chat (do not skip):** After each `notion-update-page` or `notion-create-pages`, output the modified content in chat. You already have it (e.g. `new_str`, `properties`)—no `notion-fetch` needed. Follow `notion-output-after-write` skill for format (Original → Modified).
- **Retry on failure**: If a Notion MCP call fails due to connection/disconnection, retry per `Core/notion-retry.mdc` (max 2 retries, 5–10 s delay) before reporting failure.

## Token Optimization

- **Read**: Only when user mentions project name, says "continue", "load context", or at command start. Fetch once per session when possible.
- **Write**: Only when user explicitly triggers (e.g. "update memory bank", "save progress") or at end of /van, /plan, /creative, /build, /reflect, /archive.
- **Active Context writes:** Not every Memory Bank write command must update **Active Context**; follow **`## Active Context: Notion policy and multi-task`** (**When to write**) so `/build` and `/creative` do not bulk-log there by default.
